      "writtenOn": "2026-10-27T10:26:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This array of objects here looks like it would conflict with the PDI patch\n\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/+/96007/1\n\nIf we want to have it in PDI then the generated client/server should be able to access all properties from the schema.\n\nWith how it\u0027s written here and current EM implementation, the nested objects would go on separate D-Bus interfaces and be unavailable to the generated client, meaning they would have to fetch them via another way, defeating the purpose of having a generated code.\n\nThe quick fix could be to flatten it as `Names` and `SensorIDs` (array of string and array of integer) which is compatible with 96007.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 18,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "f19bd01a4bd29b49b7cbc0fd2cce6071275bdcee",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
