      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T07:45:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Following up on my question about devices behind a USB bridge: I\u0027ve posted a [design for MCTP device discovery](https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/docs/+/96378) that proposes a `PLDMTerminus` entry on the device\u0027s board for settings like these, since a device behind a bridge has no transport record of its own. That would also keep `MCTPI2CTarget` describing only the transport, as in [its PDI definition](https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/+/96007). I\u0027d welcome your view on it before the property settles here.",
      "parentUuid": "973fb0ba_1ce4d797",
